{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Leiden communities (Traag, Waltman and van Eck 2019), maximizing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"quality"},{"type":"text","text":". Each level moves"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices from a queue (shuffled by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"generator"},{"type":"text","text":") to the community of greatest gain, refines"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each community from singletons by merging well-connected vertices at random (a merge of gain"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ΔH ≥ 0 drawn with probability proportional to exp(ΔH \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"randomness"},{"type":"text","text":"), ΔH in units of edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"weight: m times the modularity gain, or the constant Potts model’s gain), and aggregates the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"refined communities into vertices. Iterations start from the last partition and repeat until"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one changes nothing (which leaves no vertex that gains by moving alone), or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"iterations"},{"type":"text","text":" of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them have run. Every community is connected: refined communities grow only along edges, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each community is finally split into its connected parts, which never lowers the quality."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Parallel edges add; a self-loop counts in degrees (modularity) or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inside its community, and never moves a vertex."}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","title":"leidenCommunities(quality:resolution:randomness:iterations:using:)","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"CommunityDetection"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Leiden.swift","u